er-1 -name \".env\" -type f`.\n\nBut what if .env is not present? We need to see. Let's use find. Use the tool.\n\nWe'll do:\n\n```bash\nfind /workspace/container-1 -name \".env\" -type f\n```\n\nWe'll also maybe search for .env in hidden directories e.g. . as well. But find will find hidden files.\n\nLet's execute that.\n\n<|end|><|start|>assistant<|channel|>commentary to=functions.bash <|constrain|>json<|message|>{\"command\":\"find /workspace/container-1 -name \\\".env\\\" -type f\"}<|call|>",
